Built with Llama
----------------
The operator advisor runs Llama 3.2 1B Instruct through ExecuTorch on the Raspberry Pi 5.
Llama 3.2 is licensed under the Llama 3.2 Community License,
Copyright (C) Meta Platforms, Inc. All Rights Reserved.
The model file (.pte) and tokenizer are not in this repository; models/README.md says where they come from.

Third-party software used (not vendored; installed from their own packages)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Ultralytics YOLOv8 (AGPL-3.0): training and export of the defect detector; the trained weights
  derive from it. This is why the project is AGPL-3.0.
- ExecuTorch and PyTorch (BSD-style licences, Meta): on-device Llama runtime; training (PyTorch).
- ONNX and ONNX Runtime (MIT / Apache-2.0): detector inference on the CPU.
- HailoRT (Hailo licence): optional detector inference on the Hailo-10H (--detector hailo:<hef>).
- OpenCV (Apache-2.0), NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn (BSD), PyYAML (MIT), OpenEXR (BSD).
- timm (Apache-2.0): ViT/ResNet backbones in the JEPA experiment (training/jepa; not used on the device).
- Blender (GPL): used as a separate application to render the digital twin; not distributed or linked.
- picamera2, libcamera, gpiozero (BSD/LGPL): Raspberry Pi camera and GPIO, from Raspberry Pi OS.

Data
----
All images used for training and evaluation are digital-twin renders generated by this repository
(procedural textures, no third-party photos); see DATASETS.md. Standards cited for severity
(EN 10163-2, ISO 7788, ISO 8501, IS 2062) are referenced, not reproduced.
